geLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="kpi_107"><mxGeometry x="0.82" y="-9" relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="kpi_110" value="set_by" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="kpi_107"><mxGeometry x="0.5" y="-9" relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="kpi_111" value="&lt;b&gt;Each indicator is its own class&lt;/b&gt; (Single Responsibility: one reason to change). &lt;i&gt;KpiService&lt;/i&gt; only loops over &lt;i&gt;KpiIndicator&lt;/i&gt; objects and applies the weights, so it depends on the abstraction, not on seven formulas (Dependency Inversion).&lt;br&gt;This matters for NSP because the CEO said the indicator mix “should be further researched and fine tuned” (interview Q8): adding or replacing an indicator is one new class.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Composition:&lt;/b&gt; a snapshot's scores and a weight set's weights are locked together and never shared." style="fontFamily=Helvetica;html=1;shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#b59b2b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#3d3300;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="190" y="250" width="296" height="212" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="retention" name="C2 Dropout risk"><mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="700" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1400" pageHeight="930" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="retention_2" value="&lt;b&gt;Class diagram 4 – dropout risk and retention&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#666666'&gt;UC-03 View Dropout Risk Dashboard · gr